From 2703921712a265a33d5180ec19efc217ca060543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 11:01:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06891/11362] [outer-loop] ARC re86 round-6: honest null, rules
 out a route-shortcut hypothesis

Round-6 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on re86 tested whether round-5's
per-fixture flatten/paint steps are strictly necessary, or whether each
rectangle could skip straight to the corridor/compress/cross/restore
sequence (170 actions vs round-5's 269). This shortened route did NOT
trigger a win -- confirms the per-fixture paint steps are load-bearing,
not incidental overhead. A negative finding, not new route progress.

A live-frame diagnostic crashed mid-session (its own tooling, not a game
issue), ending the run early.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 7. Next
attempt should return to round 5's full per-fixture route for the second
rectangle's crossing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
